#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:349
msgid "Monitor all node parameters simultaneously"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:351
msgid ""
"If you need to monitor multiple nodes or parameters at the same time, it "
"would be cumbersome to have to call ``add_parameter_callback`` once for each "
"of them. In this case, you can use ``add_parameter_event_callback`` to "
"register a single callback that fires when *any* parameters of *any* nodes "
"change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:354
msgid ""
"To do this, first update the SampleNodeWithParameters constructor to add the "
"following code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:356
msgid ""
"this->declare_parameter(\"another_double_param\", 0.0);\n"
"\n"
"...\n"
"\n"
"auto event_cb = [this](const rcl_interfaces::msg::ParameterEvent & "
"parameter_event) {\n"
"    RCLCPP_INFO(\n"
"      this->get_logger(), \"Received parameter event from node \\\"%s\\"
"\"\",\n"
"      parameter_event.node.c_str());\n"
"\n"
"    for (const auto& p : parameter_event.changed_parameters) {\n"
"      RCLCPP_INFO(\n"
"        this->get_logger(), \"Inside event: \\\"%s\\\" changed to %s\",\n"
"        p.name.c_str(),\n"
"        rclcpp::Parameter::from_parameter_msg(p).value_to_string()."
"c_str());\n"
"    };\n"
"  };\n"
"event_cb_handle_ = param_subscriber_->add_parameter_event_callback(event_cb);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:376
msgid ""
"This declares a new double parameter ``another_double_param`` and adds an "
"event callback that will monitor both parameters. Note that the "
"``parameter_event`` is of type `rcl_interfaces/msg/ParameterEvent <https://"
"docs.ros.org/en/rolling/p/rcl_interfaces/msg/ParameterEvent.html>`_. "
"Although it's not shown in this tutorial, event callbacks can also be used "
"to monitor when parameters are added or deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:380
msgid ""
"Finally, don't forget to add the event callback handle as a private member:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:382
msgid ""
"private:\n"
"  ...\n"
"  std::shared_ptr<rclcpp::ParameterEventCallbackHandle> event_cb_handle_;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:388
msgid ""
"Navigate back to the root of your workspace, ``ros2_ws``, and rebuild your "
"updated package as before:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:412
msgid "$ call install\\setup.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:416
msgid ""
"To test the new event callback, first run the parameter_event_handler node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:422
msgid ""
"Then, from a second terminal (with ROS sourced), let's set the original int "
"parameter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:424
msgid "$ ros2 param set node_with_parameters an_int_param 44"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:428
msgid ""
"Upon executing this command, you should see both the single-parameter "
"callback, as well as the event callback being fired:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:430
msgid ""
"[INFO] [1747144403.418980063] [node_with_parameters]: cb: Received an update "
"to parameter \"an_int_param\" of type integer: \"44\"\n"
"[INFO] [1747144403.419086611] [node_with_parameters]: Received parameter "
"event from node \"/node_with_parameters\"\n"
"[INFO] [1747144403.419114103] [node_with_parameters]: Inside event: "
"\"an_int_param\" changed to 44"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:436
msgid "Now set the new double parameter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:438
msgid "$ ros2 param set node_with_parameters another_double_param 4.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:442
msgid ""
"Since no single-parameter callback was added (via "
"``add_parameter_callback``) for the double parameter, we should see only the "
"event callback fire:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:444
msgid ""
"[INFO] [1747144452.917437113] [node_with_parameters]: Received parameter "
"event from node \"/node_with_parameters\"\n"
"[INFO] [1747144452.917591649] [node_with_parameters]: Inside event: "
"\"another_double_param\" changed to 4.400000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:451
msgid ""
"When setting multiple parameters at once, it's best to use "
"``set_parameters_atomically``, explained in :doc:`../../About-Parameters`. "
"This way, the event callback is only fired once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:455
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-CPP.rst:457
msgid ""
"You created a node with a parameter and used the ParameterEventHandler class "
"to set a callback to monitor changes to that parameter. You also used the "
"same class to monitor changes to a remote node, and to monitor all "
"parameters in a single event callback. The ParameterEventHandler is a "
"convenient way to monitor for parameter changes so that you can then respond "
"to the updated values."
msgstr ""

